{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' __issue_context__.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"**CL term**\\n[CL_0000999](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000999) — CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell\\n\\n**Suggested revision of class hierarchy**\\nChange the Equivalent To class from `conventional dendritic cell` to [CD11b-positive dendritic cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002465).\\n\\n**Rationale**  \\nCurrently, CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0000999) has `conventional dendritic cell` as its Equivalent To class. We propose changing it to CD11b-positive dendritic cell. This change reflects a more natural hierarchical relationship, as CD11b-positive dendritic cell represents a parent concept encompassing CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell.\\n\\nA concrete example supporting this change is already present in the ontology: CD4-negative, CD8-alpha-negative, CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0002454) uses CD11b-positive dendritic cell as its Equivalent To class. Applying the same principle here ensures consistency and aligns with existing ontology modeling practices.\\n\\nThank you for your consideration.\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"[Class hierarchy] CD4+ CD11b+ dendritic cell [CL_0000999]: Change parent to CD11b+ DC\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3379\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
